Cell["\<\
Of course, the data tells us the proportions of households that we expect the \
distribution to predict for earning amounts between the cutoff values. For \
example, the proportion of households with earnings between $10000 and $15000 \
should be 0.043. Thus, we\[CloseCurlyQuote]ll try to minimize the mean \
squared error given by following objective function.\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.833090238004571*^9, 3.8330902452721987`*^9}, {
  3.833090278582087*^9, 
  3.833090467372319*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"fed5d366-6cde-45a4-82ac-\
932f40935d0c"],

